    "87f0aecd-dfce-498a-9ff1-80a32180dcaa": {
      "id": "87f0aecd-dfce-498a-9ff1-80a32180dcaa",
      "name": "Components",
      "content": "<p></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "54647fdc-d197-4733-8ccf-5bbda1368ab9",
      "childrenIds": [
        "8e5de290-2053-4b72-8ee7-af4f4cde6deb"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "2.1"
    },
    "8e5de290-2053-4b72-8ee7-af4f4cde6deb": {
      "id": "8e5de290-2053-4b72-8ee7-af4f4cde6deb",
      "name": "Electron Platform",
      "content": "<p>The Electron platform forms a critical component within the IdeaM Development environment, serving as the foundation for building cross-platform desktop applications. Choosing Electron allows IdeaM to leverage web technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to create applications that can run seamlessly on Windows, macOS, and Linux. This approach significantly reduces development time and costs compared to maintaining separate native codebases for each operating system. The Electron platform within IdeaM incorporates pre-configured build scripts, testing frameworks, and deployment pipelines specifically tailored for the IdeaM architecture. This standardization ensures consistency across all desktop applications developed within the environment and simplifies the integration of new features and updates. Furthermore, the Electron platform is continuously monitored and updated to ensure compatibility with the latest operating system versions and security patches, providing a stable and secure foundation for IdeaM's desktop offerings. The use of Electron also allows for easy integration with web services and APIs, enabling IdeaM applications to connect to cloud-based resources and access a wider range of functionalities.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "87f0aecd-dfce-498a-9ff1-80a32180dcaa",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "2.1.1"
    },
    "2018175e-157f-43a4-a9a0-a26acc0a9b55": {
      "id": "2018175e-157f-43a4-a9a0-a26acc0a9b55",
      "name": "Developers Guide",
      "content": "<h1>Developers Guide</h1><p>The Developer's Guide is the central resource for programmers looking to extend, customize, or integrate with the IdeaM platform. This comprehensive guide provides detailed information on the IdeaM API, outlining available endpoints, data structures, authentication methods, and best practices for building robust and reliable integrations. It covers everything from simple data retrieval to complex workflow automation, offering code examples in various programming languages to accelerate development. Beyond the API, the guide also delves into the IdeaM architecture, explaining the core components and their interactions, allowing developers to understand the underlying system and tailor their solutions accordingly. Furthermore, it provides guidance on contributing to the IdeaM open-source community, detailing the contribution process, coding standards, and testing procedures. The Developer's Guide is a living document, constantly updated with new features, improvements, and community contributions, ensuring developers have access to the latest information and can leverage the full power of the IdeaM platform.</p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "17a29ec6-74ba-4196-8f2f-f7dc8a59f862",
      "childrenIds": [
        "6db29670-50f8-4bf1-8195-ec33040202e4"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": true,
      "prefix": "3"
    },
    "6db29670-50f8-4bf1-8195-ec33040202e4": {
      "id": "6db29670-50f8-4bf1-8195-ec33040202e4",
      "name": "Mission",
      "content": "<p>How to continue IdeaM development while propagating all changes to GIT and restore all Multiplatform functionality. Including:</p><p></p><p><strong>Multi-Platform Distribution</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Web Platform</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbs