      "name": "All outlines backup/restore",
      "content": "<p>⏺ Perfect! The feature is now deployed and will be available in your apps shortly.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>How to Transfer Your Outlines:</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Step 1: Backup from Safari WebApp</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 1. Open your <strong>Safari WebApp</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Click the <strong>outline dropdown menu</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 3. Find the new <strong>\"Backup &amp; Restore\"</strong> section&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 4. Click <strong>\"Backup All Outlines\"</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 5. A file downloads to Downloads folder (e.g., idiampro_backup_2025-12-28T03-45-12.json)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Step 2: Restore in Dev App</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 1. Open <strong>IdeaM Dev</strong> (Electron) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Click the <strong>outline dropdown menu</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 3. Click <strong>\"Restore All Outlines\"</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 4. Select the backup file you just downloaded &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 5. All your outlines appear! ✓&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Step 3: Set up iCloud (Optional)</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 1. In Dev app: Settings → Select iCloud folder&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Now everything auto-saves to iCloud&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; The feature will appear in your apps: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Safari WebApp</strong>: Within 60 seconds (update notification) or restart &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Dev App</strong>: Refresh with Cmd+R &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; Try it once the update notification appears! Your massive \"IdeaM Development\" outline will transfer in seconds.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "2f759835-9c75-462e-9901-4509889e81e2",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "6.3"
    },
    "54647fdc-d197-4733-8ccf-5bbda1368ab9": {
      "id": "54647fdc-d197-4733-8ccf-5bbda1368ab9",
      "name": "Architecture",
      "content": "<p></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "17a29ec6-74ba-4196-8f2f-f7dc8a59f862",
      "childrenIds": [
        "87f0aecd-dfce-498a-9ff1-80a32180dcaa",
        "0dee917f-13f5-4e20-8049-06fb711d32a6",
        "45082891-6905-4755-8718-a99944d7656d",
        "platform-strategy-runs-where-2026-07-12"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "2"
    },
    "0dee917f-13f5-4e20-8049-06fb711d32a6": {
      "id": "0dee917f-13f5-4e20-8049-06fb711d32a6",
      "name": "Outline Storage",
      "content": "<p>Here's where each app stores data:</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; | App &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Storage Location&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |</p><p>&nbsp; |---------------|-----------------------------------------------------|</p><p>&nbsp; | Safari Webapp | Browser localStorage (not files)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |</p><p>&nbsp; | Desktop App &nbsp; | Electron localStorage OR files (if folder selected) |</p><p>&nbsp; | Dev App &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Electron localStorage OR files (if folder selected) |</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "54647fdc-d197-4733-8ccf-5bbda1368ab9",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "2.2"
    },
    "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142": {
      "id": "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142",
      "name": "App store submission",
      "content": "<p>App store submission is the crucial final step in making your application available to a wider audience. While I can handle the majority of the preparatory work, the actual submission process requires your direct involvement due to the need for your personal developer account credentials. This involves logging into platforms like App Store Connect (for Apple's App Store) to initiate the submission and manage the app's listing. My role is to ensure that your application is fully compliant with the store's guidelines and technically ready for review, minimizing the risk of rejection and streamlining the overall submission process. I will meticulously configure the build settings, handle code signing and notarization (where applicable), and provide you with all the necessary assets and metadata to create a compelling and informative app listing.<br></p><p>Claude: I can help you <strong>prepare</strong> everything for app store submission, but the actual submission requires your personal login to developer accounts. Here's what's involved:</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>What I can do:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Configure Electron Builder for production builds</p><p>&nbsp; - Set up code signing configuration</p><p>&nbsp; - Create app icons in all required sizes</p><p>&nbsp; - Generate screenshots for store listings</p><p>&nbsp; - Write app descriptions and metadata</p><p>&nbsp; - Configure notarization for macOS</p><p>&nbsp; - Set up auto-updates</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>What you'll need:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Apple Developer Account</strong> ($99/year) for Mac App Store</p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Apple ID</strong> with 2FA for signing and notarization</p><p>&nbsp; - You'll click \"Submit\" in App Store Connect (requires your login)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Optional stores:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Microsoft Store (Windows)</p><p>&nbsp; - Snapcraft/Flathub (Linux)</p><p>&nbsp; - Direct download from your website (no store needed)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp;Would you like me to start preparing the build configuration? We can do a direct download release first (simpler) before tackling App Store submission.</p><p></p><p></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "17a29ec6-74ba-4196-8f2f-f7dc8a59f862",
      "childrenIds": [
        "c532b50b-823b-4309-b717-2ec786dc73a2",
        "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
        "54cc09ae-6bc3-42e5-a415-3bb3170e001d",
        "55b7c505-c1bb-4c96-823a-71dea3b8a6a7"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": true,
      "prefix": "10"
    },
    "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d": {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "name": "TestFlight Beta Distribution",
      "content": "<p><strong>TestFlight Beta Distribution — Established March 2026</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>What is TestFlight?</strong></p><p>TestFlight is Apple's official app for distributing beta (pre-release) versions of apps to testers. Think of it like a private App Store just for your team. Instead of plugging each device into your Mac with a cable, you upload the app once and everyone downloads it wirelessly — just like installing an app from the App Store.</p><p></p><p><strong>Why we use it:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Install IdeaM on any iPhone, iPad, or Mac without cables</p></li><li><p>Push updates wirelessly — testers just tap \"Update\" in the TestFlight app</p></li><li><p>Add new testers by simply sending them an email invitation</p></li><li><p>Each build stays available for 90 days</p></li></ul><p></p><hr><p><strong>How the workflows fit together:</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>ONE-TIME SETUP (do these once, then never again):</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Set up prerequisites</strong> (10.2.1) — Get your developer account, install Xcode, accept agreements</p></li><li><p><strong>Register the app</strong> (10.2.2) — Tell Apple that IdeaM exists</p></li><li><p><strong>Connect each device once</strong> (10.2.3) — Plug in each iPhone/iPad via cable so Xcode can register it</p></li><li><p><strong>Set up your test group</strong> (10.2.6) — Create a group in App Store Connect and add testers by email</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>FIRST BUILD (do these to get the app on your devices the first time):</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Create an archive</strong> (10.2.4) — Package the app in Xcode</p></li><li><p><strong>Upload the build</strong> (10.2.5) — Send the packaged app to Apple</p></li><li><p><strong>Install on each device</strong> (10.2.7) — Open TestFlight on the device and tap Install</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>EVERY UPDATE (repeat these whenever you change the app):</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Create a new archive</strong> (10.2.4) — Package the updated app</p></li><li><p><strong>Upload the new build</strong> (10.2.5) — Send it to Apple</p></li><li><p><strong>Update on each device</strong> (10.2.8) — Open TestFlight and tap Update</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>AS NEEDED (reference these when something goes wrong):</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Fix app icon issues</strong> (10.2.9) — If the upload fails because of the icon</p></li><li><p><strong>Fix common problems</strong> (10.2.10) — Look up error messages and solutions</p></li><li><p><strong>Check deployment status</strong> (10.2.11) — See which devices have the app and when builds expire</p></li></ul><p></p><hr><p></p><p><strong>Key terms:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Build</strong> — A packaged version of the app, ready to install. Each time we make changes and want to test them, we create a new build.</p></li><li><p><strong>Archive</strong> — The process of packaging the app into a build. Done in Xcode (Apple's development tool).</p></li><li><p><strong>App Store Connect</strong> — Apple's website where you manage your apps, testers, and builds. This is where TestFlight lives.</p></li><li><p><strong>Internal Tester</strong> — Someone on your developer team who can install beta builds. Limited to 100 people.</p></li><li><p><strong>Bundle ID</strong> — A unique name that identifies your app to Apple (ours is com.idiampro.app). Like a Social Security number for the app.</p><div src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"\" data-image-block=\"\" data-image-src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" data-image-alt=\"\"></div></li></ul><p></p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142",
      "childrenIds": [
        "tf-child-01-prerequisites",
        "tf-child-02-app-store-connect",
        "tf-child-03-register-device",
        "tf-child-04-create-archive",
        "tf-child-05-upload-build",
        "tf-child-06-configure-testflight",
        "tf-child-07-install-on-device",
        "tf-child-08-push-update",
        "tf-child-09-app-icon",
        "tf-child-10-troubleshooting",
        "tf-child-11-status"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2"
    },
    "tf-child-01-prerequisites": {
      "id": "tf-child-01-prerequisites",
      "name": "Set Up These Prerequisites First (One-Time Only)",
      "content": "<p><strong>Do this once before your first TestFlight upload.</strong> After completing these steps, you won't need to repeat them.</p><p></p><p><strong>1. Get a paid Apple Developer Account</strong></p><p>Go to developer.apple.com/account and sign up for the Apple Developer Program ($99/year). A free Apple ID is not enough — you must have the paid membership to use TestFlight. Once enrolled, Apple assigns you a Team ID (ours is RRXN3CLBJH) — you don't need to memorize this, but it's how Apple identifies your account.</p><p></p><p><strong>2. Install Xcode on your Mac</strong></p><p>Open the Mac App Store, search for \"Xcode,\" and download it. Xcode is Apple's free development tool that we use to package and upload the app. It's a large download (several GB), so plan accordingly.</p><p></p><p><strong>3. Connect at least one device to your Mac with a cable</strong></p><p>Plug in any iPhone or iPad via USB at least once so Xcode can register it with your developer account. After this first cable connection, all future distribution happens wirelessly through TestFlight.</p><p></p><p><strong>4. Accept the iOS Paid Apps Agreement</strong></p><p>Go to appstoreconnect.apple.com, navigate to the Business section, and accept the \"iOS Paid Apps\" agreement. If it says \"expired,\" follow the on-screen prompts to renew it. Also fill in your tax and banking information when asked — Apple requires this before you can distribute apps.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.1"
    },
    "tf-child-02-app-store-connect": {
      "id": "tf-child-02-app-store-connect",
      "name": "Register Your App in App Store Connect",
      "content": "<p><strong>Tell Apple your app exists so you can start uploading builds.</strong> You only need to do this once.</p><p></p><p><strong>Follow these steps:</strong></p><ol><li><p>Open your browser and go to appstoreconnect.apple.com</p></li><li><p>Sign in with your Apple Developer account</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Apps</strong> in the top menu</p></li><li><p>Click the <strong>\"+\" button</strong> to create a new app</p></li><li><p>Fill in the form:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Platform:</strong> Select iOS and macOS</p></li><li><p><strong>Name:</strong> Type \"IdeaM\" — this is the name users will see</p></li><li><p><strong>Primary Language:</strong> Choose English</p></li><li><p><strong>Bundle ID:</strong> Pick com.idiampro.app from the dropdown. (A Bundle ID is a unique name that identifies your app to Apple, like a Social Security number for the app.) If you don't see it in the dropdown, you need to register it first — go to developer.apple.com → Certificates, Identifiers &amp; Profiles → Identifiers and add it there.</p></li><li><p><strong>SKU:</strong> Type \"idiampro\" — this is just an internal code for your own bookkeeping, nobody else ever sees it</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Click <strong>Create</strong></p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Skip the marketing fields.</strong> Don't worry about promotional text, descriptions, screenshots, or pricing. None of that is needed for TestFlight — it's only required later if you publish to the public App Store.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.2"
    },
    "tf-child-03-register-device": {
      "id": "tf-child-03-register-device",
      "name": "Connect and Register a New Device",
      "content": "<p><strong>Connect each new device to your Mac once so Apple knows it's authorized.</strong> After this one-time cable connection, all future app distribution happens wirelessly through TestFlight.</p><p></p><p><strong>Before you start, do these three things on the device:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Unlock the device</strong> — leave it on the Home Screen</p></li><li><p><strong>Turn on Developer Mode</strong> — go to Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Developer Mode → toggle it On. The device will ask you to restart — go ahead and restart it, then confirm when asked</p></li><li><p><strong>Grab a USB cable</strong> that connects the device to your Mac</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Now register the device:</strong></p><ol><li><p>Plug the device into your Mac with the cable (make sure the device is unlocked)</p></li><li><p>On your Mac, open <strong>Xcode</strong></p></li><li><p>Go to <strong>Window → Devices and Simulators</strong></p></li><li><p>Look for your device in the left sidebar. If it appears under \"Discovered,\" click on it and click <strong>Pair</strong></p></li><li><p>Look at your device screen — tap <strong>\"Trust This Computer\"</strong> when the prompt appears, then enter your device passcode</p></li><li><p>Wait for the pairing to finish — your device will move from \"Discovered\" to the main connected devices list</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>If the \"Trust This Computer\" prompt doesn't appear on your device:</strong></p><ol><li><p>Make sure the device is unlocked (showing the Home Screen) when you plug in</p></li><li><p>Unplug the cable and plug it back in</p></li><li><p>If it still doesn't appear, go to the device's Settings → General → Transfer or Reset → Reset → Reset Location &amp; Privacy. Don't worry — this only resets which computers the device trusts. It does NOT erase any of your data or apps. Then plug the cable back in and the prompt should appear.</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Check if wireless debugging works (optional):</strong> Unplug the cable and look at Xcode's Devices and Simulators window. If your device still appears as connected, wireless debugging is already enabled — you can push debug builds without a cable too.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.3"
    },
    "tf-child-04-create-archive": {
      "id": "tf-child-04-create-archive",
      "name": "Create an Archive (Package the App for Distribution)",
      "content": "<p><strong>Package IdeaM into a build that can be uploaded to Apple.</strong> Think of archiving like putting the app into a shipping box — it bundles everything together so it's ready to send. Do this every time you want to push a new version to TestFlight.</p><p></p><p><strong>Let Claude Code handle the prep work:</strong></p><p>Claude Code will automatically sync the latest code to the iOS project and open Xcode for you. If you're doing it yourself, ask Claude Code to run the sync and open commands.</p><p></p><p><strong>Then follow these steps in Xcode:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Verify the signing team.</strong> Click on \"App\" in Xcode's left sidebar, then click the \"Signing &amp; Capabilities\" tab. Look at the <strong>Team</strong> dropdown — make sure it says <strong>\"Howard Jachter\"</strong> (your paid account). If it says \"Howard Jachter (personal team),\" change it. The personal team won't work for TestFlight.</p></li><li><p><strong>Set the device target to universal.</strong> Find the device selector in Xcode's top toolbar (it might show a specific device name like \"iPad Mini\"). Click it and change it to <strong>\"Any iOS Device (arm64).\"</strong> This tells Xcode to build a version that works on all iPhones and iPads. <strong>Important:</strong> The Archive option stays grayed out until you select this.</p></li><li><p><strong>Start the archive.</strong> Go to <strong>Product → Archive</strong> in Xcode's menu bar.</p></li><li><p><strong>Wait for it to finish.</strong> This takes a few minutes. When done, an Archives window will pop up showing your new build with today's date and time.</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>If \"Archive\" is grayed out:</strong> Go back to step 2 — change the device selector to \"Any iOS Device (arm64).\"</p><p><strong>If you get a signing or team error:</strong> Go back to step 1 — switch to your paid developer account.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.4"
    },
    "tf-child-05-upload-build": {
      "id": "tf-child-05-upload-build",
      "name": "Upload the Build to Apple",
      "content": "<p><strong>Send your packaged app to Apple's servers so TestFlight can distribute it to all your devices.</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>Follow these steps:</strong></p><ol><li><p>In the <strong>Archives window</strong> that appeared after archiving, <strong>click on your new archive</strong> (the one with today's date and time) to select it</p></li><li><p>Click the <strong>\"Distribute App\"</strong> button on the right side</p></li><li><p>You'll see several options. <strong>Select \"TestFlight Internal Only\"</strong> — this sends the app to your private test group (up to 100 people)</p></li><li><p><strong>Click through the remaining prompts</strong>, keeping the default settings</p></li><li><p><strong>Wait for the upload to complete.</strong> You'll see \"Preparing\" then \"Uploading\" with a progress bar</p></li><li><p><strong>Look for the green checkmark</strong> and the message \"Uploaded to App Store Connect\" — that means it worked</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>What do the other distribution options mean?</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>App Store Connect</strong> — Use this only when you're ready to publish to the public App Store</p></li><li><p><strong>TestFlight Internal Only</strong> — What we use. Sends the app to your team members wirelessly</p></li><li><p><strong>Release Testing</strong> — For larger public beta tests (up to 10,000 people). We don't need this yet.</p></li><li><p><strong>Enterprise / Debugging / Custom</strong> — Special cases that don't apply to us</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What happens next:</strong> Apple takes 5-15 minutes to process the build on their servers. After that, it will appear in TestFlight and your testers can download it. You can check the processing status in App Store Connect.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.5"
    },
    "tf-child-06-configure-testflight": {
      "id": "tf-child-06-configure-testflight",
      "name": "Set Up Your Test Group and Add Testers",
      "content": "<p><strong>Tell Apple who is allowed to download your app.</strong> Apple doesn't automatically share your build with anyone — you need to create a test group and add people to it.</p><p></p><p><strong>Create a test group:</strong></p><ol><li><p>Open your browser and go to <strong>appstoreconnect.apple.com</strong></p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Apps</strong>, then click on <strong>IdeaM</strong></p></li><li><p>Click on <strong>iOS app</strong></p></li><li><p>Click the <strong>TestFlight</strong> tab in the top navigation bar</p></li><li><p>In the left sidebar, click <strong>Internal Testing</strong></p></li><li><p>Click the <strong>\"+\" button</strong> to create a new group — name it something like \"IdeaM Developer\" or \"Beta Testers\"</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Add Testers</strong> and type in the Apple ID email address of each person who should get the app (including yourself — use the same email as your developer account, e.g., hjachter@gmail.com)</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Handle the \"Missing Compliance\" notice:</strong></p><p>After Apple finishes processing a build, you'll see a yellow warning that says \"Missing Compliance — Manage.\" This is Apple asking whether your app uses encryption (they need to know for international export regulations). Don't worry, this is quick:</p><ol><li><p>Click <strong>Manage</strong></p></li><li><p>When asked about encryption type, select <strong>\"Neither\"</strong> — IdeaM only uses standard HTTPS web connections, which are automatically exempt</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Save</strong></p></li></ol><p>Once you do this, the build becomes available and your testers will receive email invitations.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.6"
    },
    "tf-child-07-install-on-device": {
      "id": "tf-child-07-install-on-device",
      "name": "Install IdeaM on Your Device",
      "content": "<p><strong>Download IdeaM onto your iPhone, iPad, or Mac.</strong> No cables needed — everything happens over Wi-Fi, just like downloading from the App Store.</p><p></p><p><strong>FIRST: Delete any existing copy of IdeaM on the device.</strong></p><p>If the device already has IdeaM installed (from Xcode via cable, or an older TestFlight build), delete it before installing. On an iPhone or iPad: long-press the IdeaM icon on the Home Screen → tap \"Remove App\" → tap \"Delete App.\" On a Mac: drag IdeaM from the Applications folder to the Trash. Skipping this step can cause the installation to freeze at about 75%.</p><p></p><p><strong>Then follow these steps on the device:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Download the TestFlight app.</strong> Open the App Store on the device, search for \"TestFlight\" (it's made by Apple), and install it — it's free</p></li><li><p><strong>Open TestFlight</strong> and sign in with the Apple ID that was added as a tester (e.g., hjachter@gmail.com)</p></li><li><p><strong>Check your email</strong> for an invitation from Apple. Look for a message titled something like \"You've been invited to test IdeaM.\" <strong>Important tip:</strong> Check your Gmail app or email provider's app — these invitations often don't show up in Apple's built-in Mail app</p></li><li><p><strong>Tap \"View in TestFlight\"</strong> in the email. This opens the TestFlight app and shows IdeaM ready to install</p></li><li><p><strong>Tap Install</strong> and wait for it to finish</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Installing on your Mac (iMac, MacBook, etc.):</strong></p><p>Since all your Macs use Apple Silicon chips, they can run iPhone and iPad apps directly. Open the TestFlight app on your Mac (download it from the Mac App Store if you don't have it), sign in with your tester Apple ID, and install IdeaM the same way. Delete any existing Electron (desktop) version of IdeaM from your Applications folder first to avoid confusion.</p><p></p><p><strong>If TestFlight asks for a \"redeem code\":</strong></p><p>You haven't been added as a tester yet. Go to App Store Connect on your Mac and add your email to the Internal Testing group (see section 10.2.6).</p><p></p><p><strong>If you see \"Unable to accept invite\":</strong></p><p>You already accepted the invitation. Just open the TestFlight app directly (don't click the email link again) — IdeaM should already be listed there.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.7"
    },
    "tf-child-08-push-update": {
      "id": "tf-child-08-push-update",
      "name": "Push an Update to All Your Devices",
      "content": "<p><strong>Send a new version of IdeaM to all your testers' devices.</strong> This is the workflow you'll repeat every time you make changes and want to test them on your iPhone, iPad, or Mac.</p><p></p><p><strong>On your Mac, do these steps:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Make your code changes</strong> — work with Claude Code as usual to add features or fix bugs</p></li><li><p><strong>Tell Claude Code to commit and push</strong> — this saves your changes and uploads the code</p></li><li><p><strong>Create a new archive in Xcode</strong> — follow section 10.2.4 (Claude Code handles the prep work for you)</p></li><li><p><strong>Upload the build to Apple</strong> — follow section 10.2.5</p></li><li><p><strong>Handle the compliance question if asked</strong> — select \"Neither\" for encryption (section 10.2.6)</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>On each device, get the update:</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Open the TestFlight app</strong></p></li><li><p>You'll see an <strong>\"Update\" button</strong> next to IdeaM</p></li><li><p><strong>Tap Update</strong> to install the latest version</p></li></ol><p></p><p><strong>Good to know:</strong> TestFlight automatically notifies testers when a new build is available, so you'll get a notification on each device reminding you to update.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.8"
    },
    "tf-child-09-app-icon": {
      "id": "tf-child-09-app-icon",
      "name": "Fix App Icon Issues",
      "content": "<p><strong>Make sure the app icon meets Apple's strict requirements, or the upload will fail.</strong></p><p></p><p>The app icon is what users see on their Home Screen, in TestFlight, and in the App Store. Apple is very particular about icon specifications — if anything is off, the upload gets rejected.</p><p></p><p><strong>Rules Apple enforces:</strong></p><ul><li><p>The main icon must be exactly <strong>1024 × 1024 pixels</strong> (pixels are the tiny dots that make up the image)</p></li><li><p>It must be a <strong>PNG file</strong> — this is a common image format, like JPEG but higher quality</p></li><li><p>It must <strong>NOT have transparency</strong> — the background must be a solid color, not see-through. In technical terms, this means \"no alpha channel.\" An alpha channel is an invisible layer in an image that controls transparency. If the icon has one, Apple rejects the upload.</p></li><li><p>All the smaller icon sizes (used for different screen sizes and contexts) must also be the correct dimensions</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>You don't need to manage icons yourself.</strong> Claude Code generates all the required icon sizes from a single master icon file. If you ever get a \"Missing app icon\" error during upload, just tell Claude Code — it will diagnose the issue (usually a wrong size or an unwanted alpha channel) and fix it automatically.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.9"
    },
    "tf-child-10-troubleshooting": {
      "id": "tf-child-10-troubleshooting",
      "name": "Fix Common Problems",
      "content": "<p><strong>Look up the error message or symptom you're seeing and follow the fix.</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>\"Missing app icon\" — upload fails</strong></p><p>Tell Claude Code about the error. The icon is either the wrong size or has transparency (see section 10.2.9). Claude Code will fix it automatically.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"No devices from which to generate a provisioning profile\"</strong></p><p>Connect at least one iPhone or iPad to your Mac with a cable and let Xcode register it (follow section 10.2.3). A \"provisioning profile\" is a digital certificate Apple creates that says \"this app is allowed to run on these specific devices.\" You don't need to understand how it works — just know that plugging in a device and registering it in Xcode solves this error.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"Archive\" is grayed out — can't click it</strong></p><p>Change the device selector in Xcode's top toolbar to \"Any iOS Device (arm64)\" instead of a specific device name. Archive only works when this universal target is selected.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"App does not have an associated developer team\"</strong></p><p>Open the project settings in Xcode: click \"App\" in the left sidebar → click the \"Signing &amp; Capabilities\" tab → change the Team dropdown to your paid developer account (\"Howard Jachter\", not the one that says \"personal team\").</p><p></p><p><strong>TestFlight asks for a \"redeem code\"</strong></p><p>You haven't been added as a tester yet. Go to App Store Connect → TestFlight → Internal Testing and add your Apple ID email to a test group (see section 10.2.6).</p><p></p><p><strong>Installation freezes at about 75%</strong></p><p>An older version of the app (installed from Xcode via cable) is conflicting with the TestFlight download. Delete IdeaM from the device first, then try installing from TestFlight again.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"Unable to accept invite\" error</strong></p><p>You already accepted the invitation earlier. Open the TestFlight app directly on the device (don't click the email link again) — IdeaM should be listed there ready to install.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"Trust This Computer\" prompt never appears on the device</strong></p><p>Make sure the device screen is unlocked when you plug in the cable. Try unplugging and re-plugging. If it still won't appear, go to the device's Settings → General → Transfer or Reset → Reset → Reset Location &amp; Privacy. This only resets which computers the device trusts — it does NOT erase data. Then plug the cable back in.</p><p></p><p><strong>Device shows under \"Discovered\" in Xcode but won't pair</strong></p><p>Turn on Developer Mode on the device: go to Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Developer Mode → toggle it On. The device will restart. After restarting, try the pairing again.</p><p></p><p><strong>\"Agreement Expired\" in App Store Connect</strong></p><p>Go to App Store Connect → click on \"Business\" → follow the prompts to renew the iOS Paid Apps agreement. You may also need to re-verify your tax and banking information.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.10"
    },
    "tf-child-11-status": {
      "id": "tf-child-11-status",
      "name": "Check Deployment Status",
      "content": "<p><strong>Track which devices have IdeaM installed and when builds expire.</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>Build History:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Build 1.0 (1)</strong> — Uploaded March 30, 2026. Expires late June 2026 (90 days from upload).</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>App Store Connect Setup:</strong></p><ul><li><p>App name: IdeaM</p></li><li><p>Bundle ID: com.idiampro.app</p></li><li><p>Platforms registered: iOS and macOS</p></li><li><p>Test group: \"IdeaM Developer\"</p></li><li><p>Tester: hjachter@gmail.com</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Device Installation Status:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>iPad Pro (M4)</strong> — Installed and working via TestFlight</p></li><li><p><strong>iPad Mini 6</strong> — Pending. Has an old Xcode-installed version that needs to be deleted first, then install from TestFlight.</p></li><li><p><strong>iPhone</strong> — Pending. Device is paired in Xcode. Open TestFlight on the phone and install.</p></li><li><p><strong>iMac (M1)</strong> — Pending. All Apple Silicon Macs can run iOS apps via TestFlight. Delete any existing IdeaM desktop (Electron) version from Applications first, then install from TestFlight on the Mac.</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Remember:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Builds expire after 90 days — upload a new build before the deadline to keep testing uninterrupted</p></li><li><p>Always delete any existing IdeaM version from a device before installing from TestFlight</p></li></ul>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "a1b2c3d4-5e6f-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.2.11"
    },
    "c532b50b-823b-4309-b717-2ec786dc73a2": {
      "id": "c532b50b-823b-4309-b717-2ec786dc73a2",
      "name": "Apple",
      "content": "<p><strong>Apple App Store Compliance Audit — March 2026</strong></p><p>Comprehensive review of IdeaM against current Apple App Store Review Guidelines, with focus on third-party dependencies, AI data sharing (Guideline 5.1.2(i)), and in-app purchase requirements.</p><p><strong>Current Status: NOT READY FOR SUBMISSION</strong></p><p>Key blockers: (1) No AI data-sharing consent flow, (2) No in-app purchase implementation, (3) Missing privacy policy/nutrition labels, (4) API key security. See child nodes for detailed findings and remediation plan.</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142",
      "childrenIds": [
        "df576dc1-6596-492a-861e-605c4d6a824e",
        "720df529-3ba7-42a9-8aba-027f543f273e",
        "271e9c43-32f5-4aa7-9593-22effed83737",
        "52345f34-eead-4d67-a51a-fcb33ace253d",
        "bf3b9fc2-5bf3-4fbd-830a-fa02a976d096",
        "ad6c413a-92ae-4f5c-8ca9-01d4e83e9330",
        "20639806-ddf9-4b6f-9f87-ac0e425cabf2"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.1"
    },
    "54cc09ae-6bc3-42e5-a415-3bb3170e001d": {
      "id": "54cc09ae-6bc3-42e5-a415-3bb3170e001d",
      "name": "Build configuration",
      "content": "<p>The build config (using Electron Builder) will:</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Create distributable apps:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - .dmg installer for Mac (drag to Applications)</p><p>&nbsp; - .exe installer for Windows</p><p>&nbsp; - .AppImage / .deb for Linux</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Handle code signing:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Signs the app so macOS doesn't show \"unidentified developer\" warnings</p><p>&nbsp; - Notarizes with Apple so Gatekeeper accepts it</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Bundle everything properly:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Packages your app with the correct Electron version</p><p>&nbsp; - Includes all dependencies</p><p>&nbsp; - Optimizes for smaller file size</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Enable auto-updates:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Users get notified when new versions are available</p><p>&nbsp; - One-click updates without re-downloading manually</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Right now</strong> you're running the dev version which loads from <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://localhost\">localhost</a>. A production build would be a standalone app that works without the dev server running.</p><p></p><p>The DMG is open. You should see the IdeaM Desktop app that you can drag to Applications.</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>What was built:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - IdeaM Desktop-1.0.0-universal.dmg (319 MB) - Installer</p><p>&nbsp; - IdeaM <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Desktop-1.0.0-universal-mac.zip\">Desktop-1.0.0-universal-mac.zip</a> (308 MB) - For auto-updates</p><p>&nbsp; - Universal binary (works on both Intel and Apple Silicon Macs)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Note:</strong> The app is <strong>not code-signed</strong> because you don't have a valid Developer ID certificate. This means:</p><p>&nbsp; - macOS will show \"unidentified developer\" warning on first launch</p><p>&nbsp; - Users can bypass with Right-click → Open</p><p>&nbsp; - For App Store or notarization, you'll need an Apple Developer account ($99/year)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>To distribute now</strong> (without signing):</p><p>&nbsp; 1. Host the DMG on your website or GitHub releases</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tell users to Right-click → Open on first launch</p><p></p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Build commands available:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - npm run electron:build:mac - macOS (DMG + ZIP)</p><p>&nbsp; - npm run electron:build:win - Windows (NSIS installer + portable)</p><p>&nbsp; - npm run electron:build:linux - Linux (AppImage + DEB)</p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.3"
    },
    "55b7c505-c1bb-4c96-823a-71dea3b8a6a7": {
      "id": "55b7c505-c1bb-4c96-823a-71dea3b8a6a7",
      "name": "Supported Platforms",
      "content": "<p><strong>macOS</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - .dmg installer (universal: Intel + Apple Silicon)</p><p>&nbsp; - .zip for auto-updates</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Windows</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - .exe NSIS installer (x64 + ARM64)</p><p>&nbsp; - Portable .exe (x64 + ARM64)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Linux</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - .AppImage (x64 + ARM64)</p><p>&nbsp; - .deb Debian/Ubuntu package (x64 + ARM64)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Web</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - Webapp via Vercel (any browser)</p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Mobile</strong></p><p>&nbsp; - iOS via Capacitor + TestFlight (iPhone, iPad)</p><p>&nbsp; - Android via Capacitor (requires Android Studio)</p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "516fed31-8ef1-4804-b052-05b47adb0142",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "10.4"
    },
    "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4": {
      "id": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "name": "Document Library",
      "content": "<h1>IdeaM Documentation</h1><p>This outline contains all the developer documentation for IdeaM.</p><h2>Quick Start</h2><ul><li><p><strong>User Workflow</strong> - 5-step guide to making changes (2 min)</p></li><li><p><strong>Responsibilities</strong> - What Claude does vs what you do (3 min)</p></li></ul><h2>Complete Guides</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Developers Manual</strong> - Complete non-technical guide (15 min)</p></li><li><p><strong>Setup Guide</strong> - Setting up a new development machine (30 min)</p></li><li><p><strong>Multi-Developer Guide</strong> - Collaborating with other developers (5 min)</p></li></ul><p></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "17a29ec6-74ba-4196-8f2f-f7dc8a59f862",
      "childrenIds": [
        "cc0a5be3-c909-4a45-a732-ada3b524e029",
        "b2ca3c4f-8dd0-4fb8-9e83-ef697cbad522",
        "417605a0-3de3-41f1-a78e-7dd414c5413f",
        "fe5cc011-8f30-40da-86e6-cffad112bb12",
        "e970b309-fcdf-4e9e-bddd-070102deb002"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": true,
      "prefix": "11"
    },
    "cc0a5be3-c909-4a45-a732-ada3b524e029": {
      "id": "cc0a5be3-c909-4a45-a732-ada3b524e029",
      "name": "Setup Guide",
      "content": "<h1>IdeaM Development Environment Setup Guide</h1><p><strong>Time Required: ~20-30 minutes</strong></p><p>This guide will help you set up a new Mac for IdeaM development.</p><hr><h2>Prerequisites</h2><h3>1. Install Homebrew (if not installed)</h3><pre><code>/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\"</code></pre><h3>2. Install Node.js (v20 or later)</h3><pre><code>brew install node</code></pre><h3>3. Install Git (usually pre-installed on Mac)</h3><pre><code>git --version  # Check if installed\nbrew install git  # Install if needed</code></pre><h3>4. Install Claude Code CLI</h3><pre><code>npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code</code></pre><hr><h2>Project Setup</h2><h3>1. Clone the Repository</h3><pre><code>cd ~/Library/Mobile\\ Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/ClaudeProjects/\ngit clone https://github.com/hjachter/IdeaM.git\ncd IdeaM</code></pre><h3>2. Install Dependencies</h3><pre><code>npm install</code></pre><h3>3. Create Environment File</h3><p>Create <code>.env.local</code> in the project root with your Gemini API key.</p><hr><h2>App Installation</h2><h3>1. Build Desktop App</h3><pre><code>npm run electron:build:mac</code></pre><p>Then open <code>dist/IdeaM Desktop-*.dmg</code> and drag to Applications.</p><h3>2. Create Dev Launcher</h3><pre><code>chmod +x start-dev.sh\nosacompile -o ~/Applications/\"IdeaM Dev.app\" -e 'do shell script \"'\"$PWD\"'/start-dev.sh &gt; /tmp/idiampro-dev.log &amp;\"'</code></pre><h3>3. Create Webapp (Safari PWA)</h3><ol><li><p>Open Safari</p></li><li><p>Go to https://idiam-pro.vercel.app</p></li><li><p>File → Add to Dock</p></li></ol><hr><h2>Quick Reference</h2><p>VersionLocationLoads FromUse ForDev~/Applications/localhost:9002DevelopmentDesktop/Applications/VercelProductionWebappDock (Safari PWA)VercelQuick access</p><hr><h2>Troubleshooting</h2><h3>Dev version won't start:</h3><pre><code>lsof -ti:9002 | xargs kill -9\npkill -f Electron\ncat /tmp/idiampro-dev.log</code></pre><p><em>Last updated: December 2024</em></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "11.1"
    },
    "b2ca3c4f-8dd0-4fb8-9e83-ef697cbad522": {
      "id": "b2ca3c4f-8dd0-4fb8-9e83-ef697cbad522",
      "name": "User Workflow",
      "content": "<h1>IdeaM Development Workflow</h1><p><strong>How to make changes to IdeaM using Claude Code</strong></p><hr><h2>Quick Workflow (5 Steps)</h2><h3>1. Start Your Session</h3><ul><li><p>Open Terminal in the IdeaM project folder</p></li><li><p>Run: <code>claude</code> to start Claude Code</p></li></ul><h3>2. Describe What You Want</h3><ul><li><p>Tell Claude what feature to add or bug to fix</p></li><li><p>Example: \"Add a dark mode toggle to the settings menu\"</p></li></ul><h3>3. Review &amp; Approve Changes</h3><ul><li><p>Claude will show you the changes it wants to make</p></li><li><p>Review and approve each change</p></li><li><p>Ask questions if anything is unclear</p></li></ul><h3>4. Test Your Changes</h3><ul><li><p>Click <strong>IdeaM Dev</strong> from Dock to test</p></li><li><p>Press <strong>Cmd+R</strong> to refresh after changes</p></li><li><p>Verify the feature works as expected</p></li></ul><h3>5. Deploy</h3><ul><li><p>Tell Claude: \"commit and push these changes\"</p></li><li><p>Claude commits to Git and pushes to GitHub</p></li><li><p>Vercel automatically deploys to production</p></li><li><p>Desktop and Webapp apps update automatically (within 60 seconds)</p></li></ul><hr><h2>What Gets Updated Automatically</h2><p>ActionDev AppDesktop AppWebappCode change (no push)Instant (Cmd+R)NoNoGit push to GitHubInstant (Cmd+R)~2 min (Vercel)~2 min (Vercel)</p><hr><h2>Tips</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Be specific</strong> - \"Add a red button\" vs \"Add a button\"</p></li><li><p><strong>Test in Dev first</strong> - Always verify before committing</p></li><li><p><strong>One feature at a time</strong> - Easier to track and revert if needed</p></li><li><p><strong>Ask Claude to explain</strong> - If code is unclear, ask!</p></li></ul><p><em>Last updated: December 2024</em></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "11.2"
    },
    "417605a0-3de3-41f1-a78e-7dd414c5413f": {
      "id": "417605a0-3de3-41f1-a78e-7dd414c5413f",
      "name": "Responsibilities",
      "content": "<h1>Claude Code vs User Responsibilities</h1><p><strong>Who does what when developing IdeaM</strong></p><hr><h2>What Claude Code Does</h2><h3>Code Work</h3><ul><li><p>Reads and understands the existing codebase</p></li><li><p>Writes new code for features you describe</p></li><li><p>Fixes bugs you report</p></li><li><p>Refactors and improves code structure</p></li><li><p>Adds tests when appropriate</p></li></ul><h3>Git Operations</h3><ul><li><p>Creates commits with descriptive messages</p></li><li><p>Pushes changes to GitHub (when you ask)</p></li><li><p>Creates branches if needed</p></li><li><p>Shows you what changed before committing</p></li></ul><h3>Problem Solving</h3><ul><li><p>Researches how to implement features</p></li><li><p>Suggests approaches and alternatives</p></li><li><p>Explains code when asked</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoots errors</p></li></ul><hr><h2>What You (The User) Do</h2><h3>Decision Making</h3><ul><li><p>Describe what features you want</p></li><li><p>Approve or reject proposed changes</p></li><li><p>Choose between alternative approaches</p></li><li><p>Decide when to commit and deploy</p></li></ul><h3>Testing</h3><ul><li><p>Click \"IdeaM Dev\" to test changes</p></li><li><p>Verify features work as expected</p></li><li><p>Report bugs or issues you find</p></li><li><p>Confirm when something works</p></li></ul><h3>Quality Control</h3><ul><li><p>Review changes Claude proposes</p></li><li><p>Ask questions if something is unclear</p></li><li><p>Request adjustments if needed</p></li><li><p>Give the final \"commit it\" approval</p></li></ul><hr><h2>Things Claude Will NOT Do Without Asking</h2><ul><li><p>Push to GitHub (waits for your \"commit\" command)</p></li><li><p>Delete important files</p></li><li><p>Make breaking changes without warning</p></li><li><p>Deploy to production without confirmation</p></li></ul><h2>Things Claude Will Do Automatically</h2><ul><li><p>Read files to understand context</p></li><li><p>Search the codebase for relevant code</p></li><li><p>Show you proposed changes before applying</p></li><li><p>Explain what each change does</p></li></ul><hr><p><em>Remember: Claude writes the code, you make the decisions.</em></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "11.3"
    },
    "fe5cc011-8f30-40da-86e6-cffad112bb12": {
      "id": "fe5cc011-8f30-40da-86e6-cffad112bb12",
      "name": "Developers Manual",
      "content": "<h1>IdeaM Developers Manual</h1><p><strong>A complete guide to developing IdeaM using Claude Code</strong></p><p><em>Written in plain language for non-programmers</em></p><hr><h2>Understanding the System</h2><h3>What is IdeaM?</h3><p>IdeaM is a professional outlining application. You don't need to know how to code. Claude Code will handle the programming for you.</p><h3>How Development Works</h3><ol><li><p><strong>You describe</strong> what you want in plain English</p></li><li><p><strong>Claude Code</strong> writes the code</p></li><li><p><strong>You test</strong> to make sure it works</p></li><li><p><strong>You approve</strong> and it goes live</p></li></ol><hr><h2>The Three App Versions</h2><p>VersionWhat It's ForWhere It Gets Data<strong>Dev</strong>Testing changes before they go liveYour computer (localhost)<strong>Desktop</strong>Daily use, full featuresInternet (Vercel)<strong>Webapp</strong>Quick access from browserInternet (Vercel)</p><h3>Important: Data is Separate</h3><p>Each version has its own storage. Use \"Backup All Outlines\" and \"Restore All Outlines\" to move data between versions.</p><hr><h2>Your Development Toolkit</h2><h3>Starting a Development Session</h3><ol><li><p>Open <strong>Terminal</strong></p></li><li><p>Type: <code>cd ~/Library/Mobile\\ Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/ClaudeProjects/IdeaM</code></p></li><li><p>Type: <code>claude</code></p></li></ol><p>You're now talking to Claude Code!</p><hr><h2>Making Changes: Step by Step</h2><ol><li><p><strong>Describe What You Want</strong> - Be specific</p></li><li><p><strong>Review Claude's Plan</strong> - Ask questions if needed</p></li><li><p><strong>Watch the Changes</strong> - Claude modifies files</p></li><li><p><strong>Test It</strong> - Click IdeaM Dev, press Cmd+R</p></li><li><p><strong>Report Results</strong> - Works or needs changes</p></li><li><p><strong>Approve for Deployment</strong> - Say \"Commit and push\"</p></li></ol><hr><h2>Backing Up Your Data</h2><h3>How to Backup</h3><ol><li><p>Open any IdeaM version</p></li><li><p>Click the dropdown arrow next to your outline name</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Backup All Outlines</strong></p></li><li><p>Save the .json file somewhere safe</p></li></ol><h3>How to Restore</h3><ol><li><p>Open the IdeaM version you want to restore to</p></li><li><p>Click the dropdown arrow</p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Restore All Outlines</strong></p></li><li><p>Select your backup .json file</p></li></ol><hr><p><em>Last updated: December 2024</em></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "11.4"
    },
    "e970b309-fcdf-4e9e-bddd-070102deb002": {
      "id": "e970b309-fcdf-4e9e-bddd-070102deb002",
      "name": "Multi-Developer Guide",
      "content": "<h1>Multi-Developer Setup Guide</h1><p><strong>How to collaborate with others on IdeaM development</strong></p><hr><h2>Overview</h2><p>If you want someone else to help develop IdeaM, here's how to set them up. Each developer works independently with their own Claude Code session, and changes are synchronized through GitHub.</p><hr><h2>Setting Up a New Developer</h2><h3>What They Need</h3><ol><li><p>A Mac computer</p></li><li><p>An Anthropic API key (for Claude Code)</p></li><li><p>GitHub access to the IdeaM repository</p></li><li><p>About 30 minutes for setup</p></li></ol><h3>GitHub Access</h3><p>The repository owner needs to:</p><ol><li><p>Go to github.com/hjachter/IdeaM</p></li><li><p>Settings &gt; Collaborators</p></li><li><p>Add the new developer's GitHub username</p></li></ol><hr><h2>How Collaboration Works</h2><h3>Before Starting Work</h3><p>Each developer should always run:</p><pre><code>git pull</code></pre><p>This downloads any changes others have made.</p><h3>After Making Changes</h3><p>Tell Claude: \"commit and push these changes\"</p><hr><h2>Avoiding Conflicts</h2><h3>The Golden Rule</h3><p><strong>Communicate about what you're working on.</strong></p><ol><li><p><strong>Coordinate:</strong> \"I'm working on the toolbar today\"</p></li><li><p><strong>Pull often:</strong> Start each session with <code>git pull</code></p></li><li><p><strong>Push often:</strong> Commit and push when done with a feature</p></li><li><p><strong>Work on different features:</strong> Don't edit the same areas</p></li></ol><hr><h2>API Keys and Secrets</h2><h3>Never Share in Code</h3><ul><li><p>Keep <code>.env.local</code> files out of Git (already configured)</p></li><li><p>Each developer uses their own API keys</p></li><li><p>Never paste API keys into chat or commits</p></li></ul><h3>Each Developer Needs</h3><ul><li><p>Their own Anthropic API key (for Claude Code)</p></li><li><p>Their own Gemini API key (for AI features in the app)</p></li></ul><hr><h2>Quick Reference</h2><h3>Start of Work Session</h3><pre><code>cd ~/Library/Mobile\\ Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/ClaudeProjects/IdeaM\ngit pull\nclaude</code></pre><h3>End of Work Session</h3><p>\"Commit and push these changes\"</p><p><em>Last updated: December 2024</em></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "99f5011b-cfe6-4e1f-a088-4936418fbff4",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "11.5"
    },
    "475d4add-6bd0-4cc8-8d23-84d84fa54c83": {
      "id": "475d4add-6bd0-4cc8-8d23-84d84fa54c83",
      "name": "Workflows",
      "content": "<p><strong>Export a single outline:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 1. Tap the <strong>outline dropdown</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tap <strong>Export Current Outline</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 3. The iOS Share sheet opens - you can:</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>AirDrop</strong> to your Mac</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>Save to Files</strong> (iCloud Drive, etc.)</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>Send via Mail/Messages</strong></p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Export all outlines:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 1. Tap the <strong>outline dropdown</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tap <strong>Backup All Outlines</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 3. Same Share sheet options</p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "17a29ec6-74ba-4196-8f2f-f7dc8a59f862",
      "childrenIds": [
        "7ab2ea20-da8b-4bf6-b158-88743a7d61b2"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": true,
      "prefix": "9"
    },
    "7ab2ea20-da8b-4bf6-b158-88743a7d61b2": {
      "id": "7ab2ea20-da8b-4bf6-b158-88743a7d61b2",
      "name": "iOS/iPadOS",
      "content": "<p></p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "475d4add-6bd0-4cc8-8d23-84d84fa54c83",
      "childrenIds": [
        "de3c91c1-702e-4912-b51d-381d76a7188a"
      ],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "9.1"
    },
    "de3c91c1-702e-4912-b51d-381d76a7188a": {
      "id": "de3c91c1-702e-4912-b51d-381d76a7188a",
      "name": "Import/Export Outlines",
      "content": "<h2>Import</h2><p>Import Outlines from local storage</p><p>&nbsp; 1. In the iOS app, tap the <strong>outline dropdown</strong> (where it shows the current outline name)</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tap <strong>Import Outline</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 3. The iOS Files picker will open</p><p>&nbsp; 4. Navigate to <strong>iCloud Drive → Documents → IDM Outlines</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 5. Select the .idm or .json file</p><h2>Export</h2><p><strong>Export a single outline:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 1. Tap the <strong>outline dropdown</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tap <strong>Export Current Outline</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 3. The iOS Share sheet opens - you can:</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>AirDrop</strong> to your Mac</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>Save to Files</strong> (iCloud Drive, etc.)</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>Send via Mail/Messages</strong></p><p></p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Export all outlines:</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 1. Tap the <strong>outline dropdown</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 2. Tap <strong>Backup All Outlines</strong></p><p>&nbsp; 3. Exportame Share sheet options</p><p></p><h2></h2><p></p>",
      "type": "document",
      "parentId": "7ab2ea20-da8b-4bf6-b158-88743a7d61b2",
      "childrenIds": [],
      "isCollapsed": false,
      "prefix": "9.1.1"
    },
    "64923839-2ac0-45b8-866d-3d7cc5343aa3": {
      "id": "64923839-2ac0-45b8-866d-3d7cc5343aa3",
      "name": "Marketing web site",
      "content": "<p>2/11/26</p><p></p><p><strong>New Site Structure:</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - / - Marketing landing page with countdown to March 2026 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - /app - The IdeaM application &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - /beta - Dedicated beta signup page with form&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - /marketing - Backup of marketing page (same content as /) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Key Features Added:</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 1. <strong>Countdown Timer</strong> - Live countdown to March 1, 2026 launch &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 2. <strong>Beta Signup Page</strong> - Full application form at /beta with:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - Name, email, role selection &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - Use case description&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - Benefits showcase (free Pro access, product input, priority support)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 3. <strong>Expanded Platform Section</strong> - Shows all targets: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>Available Now:</strong> macOS, iOS, iPad, Web&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; - <strong>March 2026:</strong> Windows, Linux, Android &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 4. <strong>\"Intelligence Amplifier\" / \"Cognitive Enhancement Platform\"</strong> branding throughout&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Regarding Affordable Hosting:</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; Your bootstrap plan recommends exactly what you have: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Vercel</strong> (current) - Free tier is very generous &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - <strong>Railway</strong> - $5/month alternative&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"http://Fly.io\"><strong>Fly.io</strong></a> - Free tier option &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; Vercel automatically deploys on push to main. Your web version is live at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"http://idiampro.vercel.app\">idiampro.vercel.app</a>.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; <strong>Note on Platform Timeline:</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; The bootstrap plan focuses on Apple + Web first, with Android later. Windows/Linux aren't in the original</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp; plan. You might want to adjust the March 2026 expectations based on development capacity - the bootstrap</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp; plan wisely suggests \"delay until revenue supports it.\"&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>✻ Cogitated for 9m 24s&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>⏺ Background command \"Find the web app URL\" completed (exit code 0) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>⏺ Read <strong>2</strong> files (ctrl+o to expand) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>⏺ That background task was from earlier - it was searching for the Vercel deployment URL. We've already &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; addressed this by:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 1. Setting up the app at /app route &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 2. Updating all \"Launch App\" buttons to navigate to /app&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; 3. The web version deploys automatically to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"http://idiampro.vercel.app\">idiampro.vercel.app</a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; The changes are live. You can test by:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - Running npm run dev and visiting <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"http://localhost:9002\">http://localhost:9002</a> to see the marketing home page &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - Click \"Try Beta Now\" to go to /app (the IdeaM application) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; - Click \"Join Beta Program\" to go to /beta (signup page)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; Or visit your deployed version at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 underline cursor-pointer\" href=\"https://idiampro.vercel.app\">https://idiampro.vercel.app</a> once Vercel finishes building.&nbsp;</p>",
      "type": "chapter",
      "parentId": "2f759835-9c75-462e-9901-4509889e81e2",
      "childrenIds": [
        "3505ea58-4d9f-420e-80e4-caf151e7df86",
